{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Amalek came.</b> From where did he come? Rather, it refers to what is written above: 'I will go to the land of Seir, from before Jacob my brother.' For Rashi explained: he departed because of the bond of debt from the decree of 'for your seed shall be a stranger,' which was imposed upon the seed of Isaac. He said: I will leave here; I have no share neither in the gift of this land given to him nor in the payment of the bond. And because of the shame that he sold his birthright to Jacob — and through this, Amalek his grandson waited until Israel departed from Egypt, and he collected the bond of debt of 'and they shall serve them and they shall afflict them four hundred years.' <b>And he fought with Israel</b> because of the hatred over the sale of the birthright. But beforehand, they were afraid to engage them, lest the payment of the bond of debt of 'and they shall serve them and they shall afflict them four hundred years' be imposed upon them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:20.106319320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}